Here's the full audit of `ProductCatalogTests.cs`:

---

## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary: 9 Critical · 1 Medium · 1 Low

This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, producing ~95% line coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs in price calculation, CSV formatting, search logic, and deletion would all slip through silently.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — False Confidence

#### 1. Coverage-touching (systemic — all 10 tests)

All 10 tests methodically call each public method on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order. 5 tests have **zero assertions**; the remaining 5 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`, which merely proves the store returned *something* — never that it returned the *right* thing. This is the single root cause of your production bugs.

#### 2. No assertions (5 tests)

| Line | Method | What goes unverified |
|------|--------|----------------------|
| 17 | `AddProduct_Works` | Was the product actually persisted? |
| 33 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | Is the price now 14.99? |
| 39 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | Is the product actually gone? |
| 64 | `GetProductCount_Works` | Is the count correct? (not even captured) |
| 69 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | Were prices actually reduced by 10%? |

**Fix — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17):**
```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

**Fix — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 33):**
```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// AFTER
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(updated);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated.Price);
```

**Fix — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39):**
```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

// AFTER
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**Fix — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 64):**
```csharp
// BEFORE
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

**Fix — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 69):**
```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);

// AFTER
